    { "id": "note-v2", "x": 0, "y": -280, "w": 340, "text": "V2 — current: canvas-first, Figma-style. No docked rail and no page header: the work surface runs edge to edge and every control floats over it as a grouped bar. Studio Home shows the nav panel pinned open, which insets the content; everywhere else it collapses to the top-left pill.", "page": "page-1" },
    { "id": "note-mirror", "x": 1520, "y": -170, "w": 340, "text": "Mirror rule (PRD 8.1): canvas LEFT, chat RIGHT — flipped from Crew Studio.\nTool rail on the left edge · history + zoom bottom-right · version/process card top-right · warnings bottom-center · toasts bottom-left · trace inspector docks LEFT of the timeline.", "page": "page-1" },
    { "id": "note-content", "x": 0, "y": -140, "w": 300, "text": "Content is the real reference crew (Mad Men poster generator). Swap copy freely — layout, components, and tokens are the spec.", "page": "page-1" },
